window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b293-269b2170bc9d6bd9.json"]={sha256:"269b2170bc9d6bd9419d4615a51f673c105331e42a9ac366d57e598903fbcbfe",value:{"id":"b293","title":"閘室節水池設計","titleEn":"Water-saving basins for lock chambers","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"節水池不是單純多建一個水槽，而是把不同高程的儲水與閘室循環連結。十個單元依序檢查幾何水量、等水位交換、位能耗散、比例分母、持續漏損、蒸發、廊道流量、交換時間、量測偏差及池體停用。所有算例均為明示假設，讓學徒能從水量與能量兩條證據鏈辨認不合理績效宣稱。","summaryEn":"Water-saving basins link storage at different elevations with the lock cycle rather than merely adding a tank. Ten units examine geometric demand, equalization, energy loss, denominators, leakage, evaporation, culvert flow, timing, measurement bias and basin outages. Declared synthetic examples give apprentices separate water and energy evidence for detecting misleading performance claims.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-lock","architectureNodes":[["閘室升降水量","Chamber lift volume"],["等水位耗散能量","Energy dissipated in equalization"],["持續漏水的日尺度","Daily leakage accounting"],["有限水頭的交換時間","Exchange time at finite residual head"],["池體停用與供水韌性","Basin outage and supply resilience"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-lock","labels":["閘室升降水量","等水位耗散能量","持續漏水的日尺度","有限水頭的交換時間","池體停用與供水韌性"],"labelsEn":["Chamber lift volume","Energy dissipated in equalization","Daily leakage accounting","Exchange time at finite residual head","Basin outage and supply resilience"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創敏感度練習：假設直壁閘室面積3000m²、升差10m、浮船排水量不變，升降水量30000m³。只把面積增加10%至3300m²，升差仍10m，水量變成33000m³。若另行假設回用率一直維持60%，外部補水由12000增至13200m³，也增加10%；但較大閘室是否仍能維持原回用率，須重新檢查節水池面積、標高、連通能力與循環時序。這裡沒有以巴拿馬尺寸作校準，也不包含漏水或鹽度沖洗。學徒應先畫控制範圍，再分開列固定假設與需要額外資料的項目，避免把幾何正比誤當整體節水保證。","textEn":"Original sensitivity exercise: assume a vertical-wall chamber of3000m² with10m lift and unchanged floating-vessel displacement, requiring30000m³. Increase only area by10% to3300m² while retaining10m lift; demand becomes33000m³. If reuse is separately assumed to remain60%, makeup rises from12000 to13200m³, also10%. Whether a larger chamber can retain that reuse fraction requires renewed checks of basin area, elevations, connections and timing. These dimensions are not calibrated to Panama and exclude leakage and salinity flushing. First draw the control boundary, then separate fixed assumptions from evidence still required; geometric proportionality is not a guarantee of whole-system saving.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b293-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「閘室升降水量」與「雙池等水位平衡」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Chamber lift volume\" and \"Two-reservoir equalization\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b293-v15-01","title":"閘室升降水量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chamber lift volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「閘室升降水量」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Chamber lift volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"船閘升降所需水量由有效水面面積與水位差決定，應先分清閘室、廊道與相連池體的控制範圍。浮船排水量若全程不變，在兩個水位狀態相減時會抵銷，不能重複扣除；不規則岸壁、跨室進出船及漏水則需要額外收支。 假設直壁閘室面積3000m²、升差10m且浮船排水量不變，ΔV=AΔh=30000m³；未計漏水與進出船交換。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閘室升降水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lift volume follows the effective waterplane area and level change after defining chamber, culverts and connected basins. A freely floating vessel with unchanged displacement cancels between the two states and must not be deducted twice. Irregular walls, vessel entry or departure and leakage require additional accounting rather than silently modifying the geometric calculation. Assume a vertical-wall chamber area3000m²,lift10m and unchanged floating displacement. ΔV=AΔh=30000m³, excluding leakage and vessel-entry exchange. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Chamber lift volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閘室升降水量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Chamber lift volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-01-k1","title":"閘室升降水量","titleEn":"Chamber lift volume","text":"船閘升降所需水量由有效水面面積與水位差決定，應先分清閘室、廊道與相連池體的控制範圍。浮船排水量若全程不變，在兩個水位狀態相減時會抵銷，不能重複扣除；不規則岸壁、跨室進出船及漏水則需要額外收支。","textEn":"Lift volume follows the effective waterplane area and level change after defining chamber, culverts and connected basins. A freely floating vessel with unchanged displacement cancels between the two states and must not be deducted twice.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘室升降水量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chamber lift volume\" is correct?","options":["浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。","船閘升降所需水量由有效水面面積與水位差決定，應先分清閘室、廊道與相連池體的控制範圍。","面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。"],"optionsEn":["The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume.","Lift volume follows the effective waterplane area and level change after defining chamber, culverts and connected basins.","Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"船閘升降所需水量由有效水面面積與水位差決定，應先分清閘室、廊道與相連池體的控制範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lift volume follows the effective waterplane area and level change after defining chamber, culverts and connected basins. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b293-v15-02","title":"閘室升降水量：定量估算","titleEn":"Chamber lift volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閘室升降水量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Chamber lift volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設直壁閘室面積3000m²、升差10m且浮船排水量不變，ΔV=AΔh=30000m³；未計漏水與進出船交換。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a vertical-wall chamber area3000m²,lift10m and unchanged floating displacement. ΔV=AΔh=30000m³, excluding leakage and vessel-entry exchange. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設直壁閘室面積3000m²、升差10m且浮船排水量不變，ΔV=AΔh=30000m³；未計漏水與進出船交換。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a vertical-wall chamber area3000m²,lift10m and unchanged floating displacement. ΔV=AΔh=30000m³, excluding leakage and vessel-entry exchange.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閘室升降水量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chamber lift volume\", which statement holds?","options":["本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。","每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock.","Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b293-v15-03","title":"閘室升降水量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chamber lift volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閘室升降水量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Chamber lift volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。將同一船舶兩狀態排水量相減，獨立列廊道及漏水項，再用水位時間序列積分對照流量，避免重複扣掉船體體積。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation. Difference the vessel displacement between states, list culverts and leakage separately, and compare integrated flow with level records without subtracting the whole hull volume twice. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。將同一船舶兩狀態排水量相減，獨立列廊道及漏水項，再用水位時間序列積分對照流量，避免重複扣掉船體體積。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation. Difference the vessel displacement between states, list culverts and leakage separately, and compare integrated flow with level records without subtracting the whole hull volume twice.","failure":"注意干擾：把浮船排水量在每次升降再扣一次會低估用水，忽略曲面閘牆則可能錯估面積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Subtracting the full vessel displacement again understates lift water, while nonvertical walls invalidate constant area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。將同一船舶兩狀態排水量相減，獨立列廊道及漏水項，再用水位時間序列積分對照流量，避免重複扣掉船體體積。","textEn":"Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation. Difference the vessel displacement between states, list culverts and leakage separately, and compare integrated flow with level records without subtracting the whole hull volume twice.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。將同一船舶兩狀態排水量相減，獨立列廊道及漏水項，再用水位時間序列積分對照流量，避免重複扣掉船體體積。","textEn":"Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation. Difference the vessel displacement between states, list culverts and leakage separately, and compare integrated flow with level records without subtracting the whole hull volume twice.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閘室升降水量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chamber lift volume\"?","options":["畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。"],"optionsEn":["Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出兩端水位與所有連通界面，核對面積是否隨高程改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw both levels and every connected boundary, checking whether area varies with elevation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b293-v15-04","title":"閘室升降水量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chamber lift volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閘室升降水量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Chamber lift volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把浮船排水量在每次升降再扣一次會低估用水，忽略曲面閘牆則可能錯估面積。模型看似守恆仍可能因控制範圍漏掉廊道而與量測持續不符。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Subtracting the full vessel displacement again understates lift water, while nonvertical walls invalidate constant area. An apparently balanced model can still disagree systematically with observations because its chosen boundary omitted culvert storage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設直壁閘室面積3000m²、升差10m且浮船排水量不變，ΔV=AΔh=30000m³；未計漏水與進出船交換。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume a vertical-wall chamber area3000m²,lift10m and unchanged floating displacement. ΔV=AΔh=30000m³, excluding leakage and vessel-entry exchange.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把浮船排水量在每次升降再扣一次會低估用水，忽略曲面閘牆則可能錯估面積。模型看似守恆仍可能因控制範圍漏掉廊道而與量測持續不符。","textEn":"Subtracting the full vessel displacement again understates lift water, while nonvertical walls invalidate constant area. An apparently balanced model can still disagree systematically with observations because its chosen boundary omitted culvert storage.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閘室升降水量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chamber lift volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把浮船排水量在每次升降再扣一次會低估用水，忽略曲面閘牆則可能錯估面積。","面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Subtracting the full vessel displacement again understates lift water, while nonvertical walls invalidate constant area.","Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把浮船排水量在每次升降再扣一次會低估用水，忽略曲面閘牆則可能錯估面積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Subtracting the full vessel displacement again understates lift water, while nonvertical walls invalidate constant area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b293-v15-05","title":"雙池等水位平衡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Two-reservoir equalization: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「雙池等水位平衡」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Two-reservoir equalization” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節水池與閘室連通後由水頭差驅動交換，若無其他流出入，最後水位可由體積守恆求得。不同面積的池體不是水位簡單平均，連通管只影響達到平衡的速度而不改變理想最終值；實際還需辨認未排盡廊道、漏水與截止閥提前關閉。 假設閘室3000m²在10m、池6000m²在4m，zf=(3000×10+6000×4)/9000=6m，轉移水量12000m³。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙池等水位平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Head difference drives exchange between chamber and basin. Without external flow, volume conservation gives the final level, weighted by surface areas rather than a simple mean. Culvert resistance affects the approach to equilibrium rather than its ideal endpoint. Real assessments must additionally identify trapped culvert volumes, leakage and valves closing before equalization is complete. Assume chamber3000m² at10m and basin6000m² at4m. Final zf=6m by area weighting, transferring12000m³ with no external flows. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Two-reservoir equalization” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙池等水位平衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Two-reservoir equalization”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-05-k1","title":"雙池等水位平衡","titleEn":"Two-reservoir equalization","text":"節水池與閘室連通後由水頭差驅動交換，若無其他流出入，最後水位可由體積守恆求得。不同面積的池體不是水位簡單平均，連通管只影響達到平衡的速度而不改變理想最終值；實際還需辨認未排盡廊道、漏水與截止閥提前關閉。","textEn":"Head difference drives exchange between chamber and basin. Without external flow, volume conservation gives the final level, weighted by surface areas rather than a simple mean.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙池等水位平衡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Two-reservoir equalization\" is correct?","options":["面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。","節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。","節水池與閘室連通後由水頭差驅動交換，若無其他流出入，最後水位可由體積守恆求得。"],"optionsEn":["Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels.","The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.","Head difference drives exchange between chamber and basin."],"answer":2,"explanation":"節水池與閘室連通後由水頭差驅動交換，若無其他流出入，最後水位可由體積守恆求得。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Head difference drives exchange between chamber and basin. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b293-v15-06","title":"雙池等水位平衡：定量估算","titleEn":"Two-reservoir equalization: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙池等水位平衡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Two-reservoir equalization” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設閘室3000m²在10m、池6000m²在4m，zf=(3000×10+6000×4)/9000=6m，轉移水量12000m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume chamber3000m² at10m and basin6000m² at4m. Final zf=6m by area weighting, transferring12000m³ with no external flows. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設閘室3000m²在10m、池6000m²在4m，zf=(3000×10+6000×4)/9000=6m，轉移水量12000m³。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume chamber3000m² at10m and basin6000m² at4m. Final zf=6m by area weighting, transferring12000m³ with no external flows.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙池等水位平衡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Two-reservoir equalization\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。","初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock.","The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b293-v15-07","title":"雙池等水位平衡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Two-reservoir equalization: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙池等水位平衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Two-reservoir equalization” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。以兩端水位變化各算一次交換體積，追查差額的時間位置，不能用任意修改池面積吸收漏水或量測偏差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections. Calculate transferred volume independently from each side, investigating when the mismatch appears instead of changing the basin area arbitrarily to conceal leakage or measurement bias. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。以兩端水位變化各算一次交換體積，追查差額的時間位置，不能用任意修改池面積吸收漏水或量測偏差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections. Calculate transferred volume independently from each side, investigating when the mismatch appears instead of changing the basin area arbitrarily to conceal leakage or measurement bias.","failure":"注意干擾：面積不同卻取水位算術平均會同時違反兩側水量，閥門未完全連通則可能在未平衡時誤判完成。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A simple level average with unequal areas violates both storage changes, while incomplete connection can mimic completion before equilibrium. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。以兩端水位變化各算一次交換體積，追查差額的時間位置，不能用任意修改池面積吸收漏水或量測偏差。","textEn":"Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections. Calculate transferred volume independently from each side, investigating when the mismatch appears instead of changing the basin area arbitrarily to conceal leakage or measurement bias.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。以兩端水位變化各算一次交換體積，追查差額的時間位置，不能用任意修改池面積吸收漏水或量測偏差。","textEn":"Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections. Calculate transferred volume independently from each side, investigating when the mismatch appears instead of changing the basin area arbitrarily to conceal leakage or measurement bias.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙池等水位平衡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Two-reservoir equalization\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。","兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections.","Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把兩個水位轉成相同基準，列出各自高程與儲量曲線並核對連通狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reference both levels to one datum and document elevation-storage curves and connections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b293-v15-08","title":"雙池等水位平衡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Two-reservoir equalization: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙池等水位平衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Two-reservoir equalization” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"面積不同卻取水位算術平均會同時違反兩側水量，閥門未完全連通則可能在未平衡時誤判完成。局部水面擺動也會讓單點讀值暫時看似相等。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A simple level average with unequal areas violates both storage changes, while incomplete connection can mimic completion before equilibrium. Local surface oscillations may also make two isolated gauge readings temporarily appear equal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設閘室3000m²在10m、池6000m²在4m，zf=(3000×10+6000×4)/9000=6m，轉移水量12000m³。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Final zf=6m by area weighting, transferring12000m³ with no external flows.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"面積不同卻取水位算術平均會同時違反兩側水量，閥門未完全連通則可能在未平衡時誤判完成。局部水面擺動也會讓單點讀值暫時看似相等。","textEn":"A simple level average with unequal areas violates both storage changes, while incomplete connection can mimic completion before equilibrium. Local surface oscillations may also make two isolated gauge readings temporarily appear equal.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙池等水位平衡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Two-reservoir equalization\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。","面積不同卻取水位算術平均會同時違反兩側水量，閥門未完全連通則可能在未平衡時誤判完成。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.","A simple level average with unequal areas violates both storage changes, while incomplete connection can mimic completion before equilibrium."],"answer":2,"explanation":"面積不同卻取水位算術平均會同時違反兩側水量，閥門未完全連通則可能在未平衡時誤判完成。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A simple level average with unequal areas violates both storage changes, while incomplete connection can mimic completion before equilibrium. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b293-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「等水位耗散能量」與「再用比例與分母」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Energy dissipated in equalization\" and \"Reuse fraction and denominator\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b293-v15-09","title":"等水位耗散能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Energy dissipated in equalization: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「等水位耗散能量」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Energy dissipated in equalization” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重力交換可回收水量但仍耗散位能，節水不等於能量無損傳遞。以共同基準計算水體位能並相減，可以分辨可用水頭和摩擦耗散；固定面積及靜止端點的理想式不含水面振盪、外部泵浦或發電回收，因此不能直接用作機組功率預測。 假設水1000kg/m³、兩池面積3000與6000m²、初水位差6m，耗散E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「等水位耗散能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gravity exchange can reuse water while dissipating potential energy, so saving water does not imply lossless energy transfer. Differencing storage potential on one datum separates available head from dissipation. The fixed-area model assumes resting endpoints and excludes surface oscillation, external pumps and energy recovery, so it cannot directly predict the output of an installed generating unit. Assume water1000kg/m³,areas3000 and6000m² and initial head difference6m. Dissipated E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ without recovery. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Energy dissipated in equalization” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「等水位耗散能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Energy dissipated in equalization”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-09-k1","title":"等水位耗散能量","titleEn":"Energy dissipated in equalization","text":"重力交換可回收水量但仍耗散位能，節水不等於能量無損傳遞。以共同基準計算水體位能並相減，可以分辨可用水頭和摩擦耗散；固定面積及靜止端點的理想式不含水面振盪、外部泵浦或發電回收，因此不能直接用作機組功率預測。","textEn":"Gravity exchange can reuse water while dissipating potential energy, so saving water does not imply lossless energy transfer. Differencing storage potential on one datum separates available head from dissipation.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「等水位耗散能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Energy dissipated in equalization\" is correct?","options":["重力交換可回收水量但仍耗散位能，節水不等於能量無損傳遞。","節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。","本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。"],"optionsEn":["Gravity exchange can reuse water while dissipating potential energy, so saving water does not imply lossless energy transfer.","The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.","Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"重力交換可回收水量但仍耗散位能，節水不等於能量無損傳遞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gravity exchange can reuse water while dissipating potential energy, so saving water does not imply lossless energy transfer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b293-v15-10","title":"等水位耗散能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Energy dissipated in equalization: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「等水位耗散能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Energy dissipated in equalization” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設水1000kg/m³、兩池面積3000與6000m²、初水位差6m，耗散E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume water1000kg/m³,areas3000 and6000m² and initial head difference6m. Dissipated E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ without recovery. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設水1000kg/m³、兩池面積3000與6000m²、初水位差6m，耗散E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume water1000kg/m³,areas3000 and6000m² and initial head difference6m. Dissipated E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ without recovery.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「等水位耗散能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Energy dissipated in equalization\", which statement holds?","options":["每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。"],"optionsEn":["Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b293-v15-11","title":"等水位耗散能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Energy dissipated in equalization: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「等水位耗散能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Energy dissipated in equalization” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。將中途動能、外部供能與可能回收分項列示，驗證能量差的去向，不把整段能量除任意時間就當設備額定功率。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity. List transient kinetic energy, external input and any recovery separately, explaining the difference rather than dividing it by an arbitrary time to claim rated machinery power. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。將中途動能、外部供能與可能回收分項列示，驗證能量差的去向，不把整段能量除任意時間就當設備額定功率。","observationEn":"Site practice: Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity. List transient kinetic energy, external input and any recovery separately, explaining the difference rather than dividing it by an arbitrary time to claim rated machinery power.","failure":"注意干擾：把回用水量當成完全回收位能會高估節能，忽略靜止端點也會漏計尚存的動能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equating reused volume with recovered potential energy overstates energy savings, and nonresting endpoints retain kinetic energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。將中途動能、外部供能與可能回收分項列示，驗證能量差的去向，不把整段能量除任意時間就當設備額定功率。","textEn":"Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity. List transient kinetic energy, external input and any recovery separately, explaining the difference rather than dividing it by an arbitrary time to claim rated machinery power.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。將中途動能、外部供能與可能回收分項列示，驗證能量差的去向，不把整段能量除任意時間就當設備額定功率。","textEn":"Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity. List transient kinetic energy, external input and any recovery separately, explaining the difference rather than dividing it by an arbitrary time to claim rated machinery power.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「等水位耗散能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Energy dissipated in equalization\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。","分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent.","Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分別積分初末兩池的重力位能，檢查使用相同零高程及總水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate initial and final potential energy for both basins using one origin and total water quantity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b293-v15-12","title":"等水位耗散能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Energy dissipated in equalization: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「等水位耗散能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Energy dissipated in equalization” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把回用水量當成完全回收位能會高估節能，忽略靜止端點也會漏計尚存的動能。兩池採不同高程原點時，計算甚至會產生沒有物理意義的能量增益。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equating reused volume with recovered potential energy overstates energy savings, and nonresting endpoints retain kinetic energy. Different elevation origins between basins can even create an apparent energy gain with no physical basis. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水1000kg/m³、兩池面積3000與6000m²、初水位差6m，耗散E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dissipated E=ρg[A1A2/(A1+A2)]Δh²/2=353.16MJ without recovery.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把回用水量當成完全回收位能會高估節能，忽略靜止端點也會漏計尚存的動能。兩池採不同高程原點時，計算甚至會產生沒有物理意義的能量增益。","textEn":"Equating reused volume with recovered potential energy overstates energy savings, and nonresting endpoints retain kinetic energy. Different elevation origins between basins can even create an apparent energy gain with no physical basis.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「等水位耗散能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Energy dissipated in equalization\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把回用水量當成完全回收位能會高估節能，忽略靜止端點也會漏計尚存的動能。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。"],"optionsEn":["Equating reused volume with recovered potential energy overstates energy savings, and nonresting endpoints retain kinetic energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把回用水量當成完全回收位能會高估節能，忽略靜止端點也會漏計尚存的動能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equating reused volume with recovered potential energy overstates energy savings, and nonresting endpoints retain kinetic energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b293-v15-13","title":"再用比例與分母：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reuse fraction and denominator: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「再用比例與分母」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reuse fraction and denominator” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節水績效必須指定基準循環、總交換量與外部補水來源，否則不同船閘大小的百分比無法直接比較。回用比例是本系統內的水量分配，和比舊船閘少用多少水屬不同問題；漏水、蒸發、鹽度控制或不同通航組合還會改變實際外部取水。 假設同一循環總交換30000m³、池回用18000m³，r=60%，外部補水12000m³；此60%不是與其他尺寸船閘的差額。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「再用比例與分母」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Performance needs a defined cycle, gross exchange and external supply, otherwise percentages from different lock sizes are not directly comparable. Reuse fraction describes internal allocation, whereas reduced water demand relative to an older lock is a different comparison. Leakage, evaporation, salt-control flushing and vessel scheduling can further change actual withdrawal beyond the nominal fraction. Assume one cycle exchanges30000m³ and reuses18000m³. Reuse is60% and external supply12000m³;60% is not a comparison with another lock size. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reuse fraction and denominator” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「再用比例與分母」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reuse fraction and denominator”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-13-k1","title":"再用比例與分母","titleEn":"Reuse fraction and denominator","text":"節水績效必須指定基準循環、總交換量與外部補水來源，否則不同船閘大小的百分比無法直接比較。回用比例是本系統內的水量分配，和比舊船閘少用多少水屬不同問題；漏水、蒸發、鹽度控制或不同通航組合還會改變實際外部取水。","textEn":"Performance needs a defined cycle, gross exchange and external supply, otherwise percentages from different lock sizes are not directly comparable. Reuse fraction describes internal allocation, whereas reduced water demand relative to an older lock is a different comparison.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「再用比例與分母」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reuse fraction and denominator\" is correct?","options":["本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。","節水績效必須指定基準循環、總交換量與外部補水來源，否則不同船閘大小的百分比無法直接比較。","沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock.","Performance needs a defined cycle, gross exchange and external supply, otherwise percentages from different lock sizes are not directly comparable.","A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"節水績效必須指定基準循環、總交換量與外部補水來源，否則不同船閘大小的百分比無法直接比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Performance needs a defined cycle, gross exchange and external supply, otherwise percentages from different lock sizes are not directly comparable. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b293-v15-14","title":"再用比例與分母：定量估算","titleEn":"Reuse fraction and denominator: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「再用比例與分母」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reuse fraction and denominator” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設同一循環總交換30000m³、池回用18000m³，r=60%，外部補水12000m³；此60%不是與其他尺寸船閘的差額。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume one cycle exchanges30000m³ and reuses18000m³. Reuse is60% and external supply12000m³;60% is not a comparison with another lock size. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設同一循環總交換30000m³、池回用18000m³，r=60%，外部補水12000m³；此60%不是與其他尺寸船閘的差額。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume one cycle exchanges30000m³ and reuses18000m³. Reuse is60% and external supply12000m³;60% is not a comparison with another lock size.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「再用比例與分母」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reuse fraction and denominator\", which statement holds?","options":["初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。","兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels.","Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b293-v15-15","title":"再用比例與分母：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reuse fraction and denominator: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「再用比例與分母」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reuse fraction and denominator” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。另記漏水和沖淡鹽分所用水，逐項核對外部取水表，避免把名義回用量當成整個流域實際節水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods. Record leakage and salinity-flushing water separately and reconcile external meters item by item instead of equating nominal reuse with actual savings across the entire watershed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。另記漏水和沖淡鹽分所用水，逐項核對外部取水表，避免把名義回用量當成整個流域實際節水。","observationEn":"Site practice: Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods. Record leakage and salinity-flushing water separately and reconcile external meters item by item instead of equating nominal reuse with actual savings across the entire watershed.","failure":"注意干擾：不同閘室總量被當成同分母時，較大的新船閘可能被錯誤宣稱節省相同比例淡水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating unequal chamber volumes as one denominator incorrectly implies proportional freshwater savings by a larger lock. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。另記漏水和沖淡鹽分所用水，逐項核對外部取水表，避免把名義回用量當成整個流域實際節水。","textEn":"Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods. Record leakage and salinity-flushing water separately and reconcile external meters item by item instead of equating nominal reuse with actual savings across the entire watershed.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。另記漏水和沖淡鹽分所用水，逐項核對外部取水表，避免把名義回用量當成整個流域實際節水。","textEn":"Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods. Record leakage and salinity-flushing water separately and reconcile external meters item by item instead of equating nominal reuse with actual savings across the entire watershed.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「再用比例與分母」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reuse fraction and denominator\"?","options":["在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。"],"optionsEn":["Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在報表中同時列出分子、分母、循環定義與船舶配置，保持比較時段一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Report numerator, denominator, cycle definition and vessel configuration for matching periods. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b293-v15-16","title":"再用比例與分母：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reuse fraction and denominator: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「再用比例與分母」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reuse fraction and denominator” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同閘室總量被當成同分母時，較大的新船閘可能被錯誤宣稱節省相同比例淡水。忽略額外沖洗用水則使內部高回用率掩蓋真正的水源負擔。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating unequal chamber volumes as one denominator incorrectly implies proportional freshwater savings by a larger lock. Omitting additional flushing allows a high internal reuse fraction to conceal the real burden on the external water source. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設同一循環總交換30000m³、池回用18000m³，r=60%，外部補水12000m³；此60%不是與其他尺寸船閘的差額。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reuse is60% and external supply12000m³;60% is not a comparison with another lock size.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同閘室總量被當成同分母時，較大的新船閘可能被錯誤宣稱節省相同比例淡水。忽略額外沖洗用水則使內部高回用率掩蓋真正的水源負擔。","textEn":"Treating unequal chamber volumes as one denominator incorrectly implies proportional freshwater savings by a larger lock. Omitting additional flushing allows a high internal reuse fraction to conceal the real burden on the external water source.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「再用比例與分母」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reuse fraction and denominator\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","不同閘室總量被當成同分母時，較大的新船閘可能被錯誤宣稱節省相同比例淡水。","沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating unequal chamber volumes as one denominator incorrectly implies proportional freshwater savings by a larger lock.","A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同閘室總量被當成同分母時，較大的新船閘可能被錯誤宣稱節省相同比例淡水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating unequal chamber volumes as one denominator incorrectly implies proportional freshwater savings by a larger lock. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b293-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「持續漏水的日尺度」與「蒸發與面積代價」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Daily leakage accounting\" and \"Evaporation and basin footprint\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b293-v15-17","title":"持續漏水的日尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Daily leakage accounting: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「持續漏水的日尺度」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Daily leakage accounting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節水池停用時仍可能因接縫或閥座漏水損失，這是持續時間問題，不能只按通航次數估算。日總量與每次循環用水需分開，且漏水隨水頭變化不一定恆定；將靜態保水觀測與運轉期間收支結合，才能判斷未解釋的補水量是否來自同一機制。 假設持續漏水0.020m³/s維持86400s，日損失Qt=1728m³；僅在漏水率固定時成立，不能由此指定現場允許值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「持續漏水的日尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Leakage through joints or seats can continue while a basin is idle, making duration as important as lockage count. Daily loss and cycle demand require separate reporting, and leakage may vary with head. Combining static retention observations with operational balances helps determine whether unexplained makeup water follows the same mechanism rather than assuming a fixed loss per vessel. Assume constant leakage0.020m³/s for86400s. Daily loss Qt=1728m³; the assumption does not specify an allowable field leakage rate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Daily leakage accounting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「持續漏水的日尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Daily leakage accounting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-17-k1","title":"持續漏水的日尺度","titleEn":"Daily leakage accounting","text":"節水池停用時仍可能因接縫或閥座漏水損失，這是持續時間問題，不能只按通航次數估算。日總量與每次循環用水需分開，且漏水隨水頭變化不一定恆定；將靜態保水觀測與運轉期間收支結合，才能判斷未解釋的補水量是否來自同一機制。","textEn":"Leakage through joints or seats can continue while a basin is idle, making duration as important as lockage count. Daily loss and cycle demand require separate reporting, and leakage may vary with head.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「持續漏水的日尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Daily leakage accounting\" is correct?","options":["沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。","每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。","節水池停用時仍可能因接縫或閥座漏水損失，這是持續時間問題，不能只按通航次數估算。"],"optionsEn":["A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock.","Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.","Leakage through joints or seats can continue while a basin is idle, making duration as important as lockage count."],"answer":2,"explanation":"節水池停用時仍可能因接縫或閥座漏水損失，這是持續時間問題，不能只按通航次數估算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Leakage through joints or seats can continue while a basin is idle, making duration as important as lockage count. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b293-v15-18","title":"持續漏水的日尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Daily leakage accounting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「持續漏水的日尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Daily leakage accounting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設持續漏水0.020m³/s維持86400s，日損失Qt=1728m³；僅在漏水率固定時成立，不能由此指定現場允許值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume constant leakage0.020m³/s for86400s. Daily loss Qt=1728m³; the assumption does not specify an allowable field leakage rate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設持續漏水0.020m³/s維持86400s，日損失Qt=1728m³；僅在漏水率固定時成立，不能由此指定現場允許值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume constant leakage0.020m³/s for86400s. Daily loss Qt=1728m³; the assumption does not specify an allowable field leakage rate.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「持續漏水的日尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Daily leakage accounting\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。","回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation.","A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b293-v15-19","title":"持續漏水的日尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Daily leakage accounting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「持續漏水的日尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Daily leakage accounting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。比較不同水頭的資料並標明觀測時長，避免將整天缺水全歸因於某一閥件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage. Compare several heads and observation lengths rather than assigning the entire daily deficit to one unverified valve defect. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。比較不同水頭的資料並標明觀測時長，避免將整天缺水全歸因於某一閥件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage. Compare several heads and observation lengths rather than assigning the entire daily deficit to one unverified valve defect.","failure":"注意干擾：高水頭短測試被外推整天可能高估損失，水位儀漂移又會假造漏水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating a brief high-head test over a day may overstate loss, while sensor drift can create fictitious leakage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。比較不同水頭的資料並標明觀測時長，避免將整天缺水全歸因於某一閥件。","textEn":"Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage. Compare several heads and observation lengths rather than assigning the entire daily deficit to one unverified valve defect.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。比較不同水頭的資料並標明觀測時長，避免將整天缺水全歸因於某一閥件。","textEn":"Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage. Compare several heads and observation lengths rather than assigning the entire daily deficit to one unverified valve defect.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「持續漏水的日尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Daily leakage accounting\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。","面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage.","Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在無進出水且水頭已知的時段追蹤池位，扣除降雨蒸發及量測偏差，再推估漏水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track level during known-head intervals without deliberate exchange, accounting for rain, evaporation and measurement bias before inferring leakage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b293-v15-20","title":"持續漏水的日尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Daily leakage accounting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「持續漏水的日尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Daily leakage accounting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高水頭短測試被外推整天可能高估損失，水位儀漂移又會假造漏水。若漏水把鹹水帶入另一池，水量問題還會伴隨水質交換而非單純消耗淡水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating a brief high-head test over a day may overstate loss, while sensor drift can create fictitious leakage. Leakage into another basin can also transport salt, producing a quality problem beyond simple freshwater consumption. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設持續漏水0.020m³/s維持86400s，日損失Qt=1728m³；僅在漏水率固定時成立，不能由此指定現場允許值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Daily loss Qt=1728m³; the assumption does not specify an allowable field leakage rate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高水頭短測試被外推整天可能高估損失，水位儀漂移又會假造漏水。若漏水把鹹水帶入另一池，水量問題還會伴隨水質交換而非單純消耗淡水。","textEn":"Extrapolating a brief high-head test over a day may overstate loss, while sensor drift can create fictitious leakage. Leakage into another basin can also transport salt, producing a quality problem beyond simple freshwater consumption.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「持續漏水的日尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Daily leakage accounting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。","高水頭短測試被外推整天可能高估損失，水位儀漂移又會假造漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.","Extrapolating a brief high-head test over a day may overstate loss, while sensor drift can create fictitious leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高水頭短測試被外推整天可能高估損失，水位儀漂移又會假造漏水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating a brief high-head test over a day may overstate loss, while sensor drift can create fictitious leakage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b293-v15-21","title":"蒸發與面積代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evaporation and basin footprint: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「蒸發與面積代價」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Evaporation and basin footprint” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"增設節水池增加可儲水量，也擴大暴露水面，日蒸發需與降雨和通航節水分開核算。實際蒸發受氣象、水溫及遮蔽影響，不能把區域年平均直接當任一日；面積計算則應依水位變動，分清池底占地和當時有效水面。 假設總水面12000m²、當日蒸發深0.005m，損失AE=60m³/day；不是每次通航都損失60m³。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「蒸發與面積代價」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Additional basins provide storage while expanding exposed surface area. Daily evaporation must be accounted for separately from rainfall and lockage savings. Weather, water temperature and shelter affect evaporation, so a regional annual average is not a value for every day. Area should follow changing levels, distinguishing the basin footprint from its actual water surface. Assume exposed water area12000m² and daily evaporation depth0.005m. Loss AE=60m³/day, not60m³ for every lockage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Evaporation and basin footprint” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「蒸發與面積代價」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Evaporation and basin footprint”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-21-k1","title":"蒸發與面積代價","titleEn":"Evaporation and basin footprint","text":"增設節水池增加可儲水量，也擴大暴露水面，日蒸發需與降雨和通航節水分開核算。實際蒸發受氣象、水溫及遮蔽影響，不能把區域年平均直接當任一日；面積計算則應依水位變動，分清池底占地和當時有效水面。","textEn":"Additional basins provide storage while expanding exposed surface area. Daily evaporation must be accounted for separately from rainfall and lockage savings.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「蒸發與面積代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evaporation and basin footprint\" is correct?","options":["增設節水池增加可儲水量，也擴大暴露水面，日蒸發需與降雨和通航節水分開核算。","每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。","初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。"],"optionsEn":["Additional basins provide storage while expanding exposed surface area.","Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.","The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels."],"answer":0,"explanation":"增設節水池增加可儲水量，也擴大暴露水面，日蒸發需與降雨和通航節水分開核算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Additional basins provide storage while expanding exposed surface area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b293-v15-22","title":"蒸發與面積代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Evaporation and basin footprint: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「蒸發與面積代價」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Evaporation and basin footprint” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設總水面12000m²、當日蒸發深0.005m，損失AE=60m³/day；不是每次通航都損失60m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume exposed water area12000m² and daily evaporation depth0.005m. Loss AE=60m³/day, not60m³ for every lockage. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設總水面12000m²、當日蒸發深0.005m，損失AE=60m³/day；不是每次通航都損失60m³。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume exposed water area12000m² and daily evaporation depth0.005m. Loss AE=60m³/day, not60m³ for every lockage.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「蒸發與面積代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evaporation and basin footprint\", which statement holds?","options":["兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。"],"optionsEn":["Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b293-v15-23","title":"蒸發與面積代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evaporation and basin footprint: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「蒸發與面積代價」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Evaporation and basin footprint” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。把每日水面積分與循環用水分欄，並比較不同季節，不把一次高溫日當成全年代表。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land. Separate daily area integration from cycle demand and compare seasons without making one hot day representative of the full operational year. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。把每日水面積分與循環用水分欄，並比較不同季節，不把一次高溫日當成全年代表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land. Separate daily area integration from cycle demand and compare seasons without making one hot day representative of the full operational year.","failure":"注意干擾：用池底面積代替斜坡池的水面可能低估蒸發，重複在每次通航扣日損失則嚴重高估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using bottom area for a sloped basin understates exposed water, while deducting daily loss at each lockage grossly overstates it. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。把每日水面積分與循環用水分欄，並比較不同季節，不把一次高溫日當成全年代表。","textEn":"Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land. Separate daily area integration from cycle demand and compare seasons without making one hot day representative of the full operational year.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。把每日水面積分與循環用水分欄，並比較不同季節，不把一次高溫日當成全年代表。","textEn":"Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land. Separate daily area integration from cycle demand and compare seasons without making one hot day representative of the full operational year.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「蒸發與面積代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evaporation and basin footprint\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。","取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.","Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land."],"answer":2,"explanation":"取得相同日期的氣象、池位及降雨資料，檢查蒸發量是否為水面而非陸地估值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match weather, level and rainfall dates and verify that evaporation represents open water rather than land. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b293-v15-24","title":"蒸發與面積代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evaporation and basin footprint: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「蒸發與面積代價」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Evaporation and basin footprint” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用池底面積代替斜坡池的水面可能低估蒸發，重複在每次通航扣日損失則嚴重高估。把降雨直接抵銷平均蒸發，還可能漏掉溢流時未能保存的雨水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using bottom area for a sloped basin understates exposed water, while deducting daily loss at each lockage grossly overstates it. Offsetting mean rainfall can also overlook water that overflowed and was never retained. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設總水面12000m²、當日蒸發深0.005m，損失AE=60m³/day；不是每次通航都損失60m³。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Loss AE=60m³/day, not60m³ for every lockage.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用池底面積代替斜坡池的水面可能低估蒸發，重複在每次通航扣日損失則嚴重高估。把降雨直接抵銷平均蒸發，還可能漏掉溢流時未能保存的雨水。","textEn":"Using bottom area for a sloped basin understates exposed water, while deducting daily loss at each lockage grossly overstates it. Offsetting mean rainfall can also overlook water that overflowed and was never retained.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「蒸發與面積代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evaporation and basin footprint\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用池底面積代替斜坡池的水面可能低估蒸發，重複在每次通航扣日損失則嚴重高估。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。"],"optionsEn":["Using bottom area for a sloped basin understates exposed water, while deducting daily loss at each lockage grossly overstates it.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用池底面積代替斜坡池的水面可能低估蒸發，重複在每次通航扣日損失則嚴重高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using bottom area for a sloped basin understates exposed water, while deducting daily loss at each lockage grossly overstates it. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b293-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「連通廊道瞬時流量」與「有限水頭的交換時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge\" and \"Exchange time at finite residual head\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b293-v15-25","title":"連通廊道瞬時流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「連通廊道瞬時流量」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"連通初期水頭差較大，流量會隨兩池水位接近而降低，固定孔口式只代表某個瞬間。閥門開度、進出口和廊道損失都會影響等效係數，慣性與水面振盪則超出準穩態模型；單一初始流量不可直接乘整段時間宣稱填池完成。 假設等效Cd=0.70、開口4m²、水頭差2m，Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s；僅作瞬時準穩態示意。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「連通廊道瞬時流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Initial head difference drives a larger flow that falls as levels converge, so a fixed-orifice relation describes one instant. Valve position, entrances and culvert losses determine the effective coefficient, while inertia and surface oscillation lie outside the quasi-steady model. Initial discharge cannot simply be multiplied by the entire exchange duration to establish completion. Assume effective Cd=0.70,opening4m² and head difference2m. Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s is an instantaneous quasi-steady illustration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「連通廊道瞬時流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-25-k1","title":"連通廊道瞬時流量","titleEn":"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge","text":"連通初期水頭差較大，流量會隨兩池水位接近而降低，固定孔口式只代表某個瞬間。閥門開度、進出口和廊道損失都會影響等效係數，慣性與水面振盪則超出準穩態模型；單一初始流量不可直接乘整段時間宣稱填池完成。","textEn":"Initial head difference drives a larger flow that falls as levels converge, so a fixed-orifice relation describes one instant. Valve position, entrances and culvert losses determine the effective coefficient, while inertia and surface oscillation lie outside the quasi-steady model.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「連通廊道瞬時流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge\" is correct?","options":["初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。","連通初期水頭差較大，流量會隨兩池水位接近而降低，固定孔口式只代表某個瞬間。","節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。"],"optionsEn":["The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels.","Initial head difference drives a larger flow that falls as levels converge, so a fixed-orifice relation describes one instant.","A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"連通初期水頭差較大，流量會隨兩池水位接近而降低，固定孔口式只代表某個瞬間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Initial head difference drives a larger flow that falls as levels converge, so a fixed-orifice relation describes one instant. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b293-v15-26","title":"連通廊道瞬時流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「連通廊道瞬時流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設等效Cd=0.70、開口4m²、水頭差2m，Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s；僅作瞬時準穩態示意。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume effective Cd=0.70,opening4m² and head difference2m. Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s is an instantaneous quasi-steady illustration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設等效Cd=0.70、開口4m²、水頭差2m，Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s；僅作瞬時準穩態示意。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume effective Cd=0.70,opening4m² and head difference2m. Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s is an instantaneous quasi-steady illustration.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「連通廊道瞬時流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge\", which statement holds?","options":["回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。","面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent.","Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b293-v15-27","title":"連通廊道瞬時流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「連通廊道瞬時流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。檢查流量是否有相位延遲或反轉，保留瞬態偏差，不用調高係數掩蓋尚未建立的流動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history. Check lag and reversals and retain transient departures rather than increasing the coefficient to conceal flow that has not yet developed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。檢查流量是否有相位延遲或反轉，保留瞬態偏差，不用調高係數掩蓋尚未建立的流動。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history. Check lag and reversals and retain transient departures rather than increasing the coefficient to conceal flow that has not yet developed.","failure":"注意干擾：初始流量外推會低估等水位時間，誤把閥位百分比當有效面積也會錯估水量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating initial discharge understates equalization time, and valve-position percentage need not equal open-area fraction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。檢查流量是否有相位延遲或反轉，保留瞬態偏差，不用調高係數掩蓋尚未建立的流動。","textEn":"Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history. Check lag and reversals and retain transient departures rather than increasing the coefficient to conceal flow that has not yet developed.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。檢查流量是否有相位延遲或反轉，保留瞬態偏差，不用調高係數掩蓋尚未建立的流動。","textEn":"Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history. Check lag and reversals and retain transient departures rather than increasing the coefficient to conceal flow that has not yet developed.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「連通廊道瞬時流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge\"?","options":["同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。"],"optionsEn":["Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步記兩端水位、閥位和流量，將等效係數適用範圍與水頭歷程畫在一起。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record both levels, valve position and discharge together, plotting coefficient applicability against the head history. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b293-v15-28","title":"連通廊道瞬時流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「連通廊道瞬時流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"初始流量外推會低估等水位時間，誤把閥位百分比當有效面積也會錯估水量。快速變動時壓力和流速不再同步，甚至可能出現準穩態式無法描述的反向流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating initial discharge understates equalization time, and valve-position percentage need not equal open-area fraction. During rapid change pressure and velocity lose synchronization and may reverse in ways the quasi-steady expression cannot represent. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設等效Cd=0.70、開口4m²、水頭差2m，Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s；僅作瞬時準穩態示意。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Q=Cd a√(2gΔh)=17.54m³/s is an instantaneous quasi-steady illustration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"初始流量外推會低估等水位時間，誤把閥位百分比當有效面積也會錯估水量。快速變動時壓力和流速不再同步，甚至可能出現準穩態式無法描述的反向流。","textEn":"Extrapolating initial discharge understates equalization time, and valve-position percentage need not equal open-area fraction. During rapid change pressure and velocity lose synchronization and may reverse in ways the quasi-steady expression cannot represent.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「連通廊道瞬時流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Instantaneous connecting-culvert discharge\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","初始流量外推會低估等水位時間，誤把閥位百分比當有效面積也會錯估水量。","節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Extrapolating initial discharge understates equalization time, and valve-position percentage need not equal open-area fraction.","A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始流量外推會低估等水位時間，誤把閥位百分比當有效面積也會錯估水量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating initial discharge understates equalization time, and valve-position percentage need not equal open-area fraction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b293-v15-29","title":"有限水頭的交換時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exchange time at finite residual head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「有限水頭的交換時間」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exchange time at finite residual head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"計算交換時間需同時更新兩個池水位，面積較小的一側變化較快，因而水頭衰減不是固定斜率。準穩態積分可到指定殘餘水頭，但接近等水位時慣性和閥門控制會更重要；模型只能提供辨識尺度，不能替實際控制系統設定關閥時刻。 假設固定池面積A1=3000、A2=6000m²、a=4m²、Cd=0.7，k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2)；水頭差Δh由6降0.1m，準穩態時間t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有限水頭的交換時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Exchange-time calculation updates both levels, with the smaller area moving faster so head does not decay linearly. A quasi-steady integral can reach a specified residual head, but inertia and valve control become important near equality. The result provides a diagnostic timescale rather than a command for closing a real valve or authorizing an operating sequence. Assume areas3000,6000m²,opening4m²,Cd=0.7. With k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2), reducing head6to0.1m takes t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exchange time at finite residual head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有限水頭的交換時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exchange time at finite residual head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-29-k1","title":"有限水頭的交換時間","titleEn":"Exchange time at finite residual head","text":"計算交換時間需同時更新兩個池水位，面積較小的一側變化較快，因而水頭衰減不是固定斜率。準穩態積分可到指定殘餘水頭，但接近等水位時慣性和閥門控制會更重要；模型只能提供辨識尺度，不能替實際控制系統設定關閥時刻。","textEn":"Exchange-time calculation updates both levels, with the smaller area moving faster so head does not decay linearly. A quasi-steady integral can reach a specified residual head, but inertia and valve control become important near equality.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有限水頭的交換時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exchange time at finite residual head\" is correct?","options":["節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。","兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。","計算交換時間需同時更新兩個池水位，面積較小的一側變化較快，因而水頭衰減不是固定斜率。"],"optionsEn":["A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation.","Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.","Exchange-time calculation updates both levels, with the smaller area moving faster so head does not decay linearly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"計算交換時間需同時更新兩個池水位，面積較小的一側變化較快，因而水頭衰減不是固定斜率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Exchange-time calculation updates both levels, with the smaller area moving faster so head does not decay linearly. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b293-v15-30","title":"有限水頭的交換時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Exchange time at finite residual head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有限水頭的交換時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exchange time at finite residual head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設固定池面積A1=3000、A2=6000m²、a=4m²、Cd=0.7，k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2)；水頭差Δh由6降0.1m，準穩態時間t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume areas3000,6000m²,opening4m²,Cd=0.7. With k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2), reducing head6to0.1m takes t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設固定池面積A1=3000、A2=6000m²、a=4m²、Cd=0.7，k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2)；水頭差Δh由6降0.1m，準穩態時間t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume areas3000,6000m²,opening4m²,Cd=0.7. With k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2), reducing head6to0.1m takes t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有限水頭的交換時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exchange time at finite residual head\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。","節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume.","The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b293-v15-31","title":"有限水頭的交換時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exchange time at finite residual head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有限水頭的交換時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exchange time at finite residual head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。對照實測水頭衰減曲線辨識係數或慣性影響，明示最後殘餘水頭，不聲稱已達實際完全平衡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases. Examine measured head decay for coefficient or inertia effects, stating the finite residual head rather than claiming that complete physical equilibrium has been achieved. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。對照實測水頭衰減曲線辨識係數或慣性影響，明示最後殘餘水頭，不聲稱已達實際完全平衡。","observationEn":"Site practice: Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases. Examine measured head decay for coefficient or inertia effects, stating the finite residual head rather than claiming that complete physical equilibrium has been achieved.","failure":"注意干擾：只更新閘室而固定池位會低估水頭衰減，導致過短交換時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Updating only the chamber while holding the basin fixed understates head decay and shortens exchange time. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。對照實測水頭衰減曲線辨識係數或慣性影響，明示最後殘餘水頭，不聲稱已達實際完全平衡。","textEn":"Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases. Examine measured head decay for coefficient or inertia effects, stating the finite residual head rather than claiming that complete physical equilibrium has been achieved.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。對照實測水頭衰減曲線辨識係數或慣性影響，明示最後殘餘水頭，不聲稱已達實際完全平衡。","textEn":"Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases. Examine measured head decay for coefficient or inertia effects, stating the finite residual head rather than claiming that complete physical equilibrium has been achieved.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有限水頭的交換時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exchange time at finite residual head\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。","沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases.","A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐步以水量守恆重算兩端水位，再與解析積分比較，確認時間步縮小後一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Update both levels by conservation and compare with the analytic integral as the timestep decreases. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b293-v15-32","title":"有限水頭的交換時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exchange time at finite residual head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有限水頭的交換時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exchange time at finite residual head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只更新閘室而固定池位會低估水頭衰減，導致過短交換時間。接近平衡仍沿用同一係數可能忽略反向振盪，因此計算終點不等於可立即解除操作連鎖。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Updating only the chamber while holding the basin fixed understates head decay and shortens exchange time. Near equality, a fixed coefficient misses possible oscillation, so the computed endpoint cannot release actual operating interlocks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固定池面積A1=3000、A2=6000m²、a=4m²、Cd=0.7，k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2)；水頭差Δh由6降0.1m，準穩態時間t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: With k=Cd a√(2g)(1/A1+1/A2), reducing head6to0.1m takes t=2(√6−√0.1)/k=688.0s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「節水池面積再小也可以在時間計算中一直當作固定水位。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A water-saving basin of any size may be treated as a fixed-level reservoir throughout the timing calculation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只更新閘室而固定池位會低估水頭衰減，導致過短交換時間。接近平衡仍沿用同一係數可能忽略反向振盪，因此計算終點不等於可立即解除操作連鎖。","textEn":"Updating only the chamber while holding the basin fixed understates head decay and shortens exchange time. Near equality, a fixed coefficient misses possible oscillation, so the computed endpoint cannot release actual operating interlocks.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有限水頭的交換時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exchange time at finite residual head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。","只更新閘室而固定池位會低估水頭衰減，導致過短交換時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.","Updating only the chamber while holding the basin fixed understates head decay and shortens exchange time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只更新閘室而固定池位會低估水頭衰減，導致過短交換時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Updating only the chamber while holding the basin fixed understates head decay and shortens exchange time. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b293-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「水位偏差與庫容」與「池體停用與供水韌性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Level bias and storage error\" and \"Basin outage and supply resilience\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b293-v15-33","title":"水位偏差與庫容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level bias and storage error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「水位偏差與庫容」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level bias and storage error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大面積節水池的水位微小偏差會轉成顯著方量，更多讀值不能自動消除共同零點誤差。位準轉換、儀器漂移及水面擺動應分別處理，庫容曲線亦需適用目前幾何；這項誤差可能使回用績效看似改善，卻沒有真正降低外部補水。 假設固定水面6000m²、共同水位偏差0.010m，庫容偏差Aδz=60m³；此系統偏差不隨讀值數增加自動消失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位偏差與庫容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A small level bias over a large basin produces substantial storage error, and more readings do not remove a shared zero offset. Datum conversion, instrument drift and surface oscillation require separate treatment, as does the validity of the current storage curve. Such error can create apparent improvement in reuse while external makeup demand remains unchanged. Assume fixed area6000m² and coherent level bias0.010m. Storage bias Aδz=60m³; additional readings do not automatically eliminate this systematic error. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level bias and storage error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位偏差與庫容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level bias and storage error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-33-k1","title":"水位偏差與庫容","titleEn":"Level bias and storage error","text":"大面積節水池的水位微小偏差會轉成顯著方量，更多讀值不能自動消除共同零點誤差。位準轉換、儀器漂移及水面擺動應分別處理，庫容曲線亦需適用目前幾何；這項誤差可能使回用績效看似改善，卻沒有真正降低外部補水。","textEn":"A small level bias over a large basin produces substantial storage error, and more readings do not remove a shared zero offset. Datum conversion, instrument drift and surface oscillation require separate treatment, as does the validity of the current storage curve.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位偏差與庫容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level bias and storage error\" is correct?","options":["大面積節水池的水位微小偏差會轉成顯著方量，更多讀值不能自動消除共同零點誤差。","兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。","回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["A small level bias over a large basin produces substantial storage error, and more readings do not remove a shared zero offset.","Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.","A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大面積節水池的水位微小偏差會轉成顯著方量，更多讀值不能自動消除共同零點誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A small level bias over a large basin produces substantial storage error, and more readings do not remove a shared zero offset. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b293-v15-34","title":"水位偏差與庫容：定量估算","titleEn":"Level bias and storage error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位偏差與庫容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level bias and storage error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設固定水面6000m²、共同水位偏差0.010m，庫容偏差Aδz=60m³；此系統偏差不隨讀值數增加自動消失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume fixed area6000m² and coherent level bias0.010m. Storage bias Aδz=60m³; additional readings do not automatically eliminate this systematic error. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設固定水面6000m²、共同水位偏差0.010m，庫容偏差Aδz=60m³；此系統偏差不隨讀值數增加自動消失。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume fixed area6000m² and coherent level bias0.010m. Storage bias Aδz=60m³; additional readings do not automatically eliminate this systematic error.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位偏差與庫容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level bias and storage error\", which statement holds?","options":["面積不同的兩個池連通後最終水位仍是原水位的算術平均。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","本船閘回用六成就表示它一定比任何舊船閘少取水六成。"],"optionsEn":["Connected basins of unequal area always finish at the arithmetic mean of their starting levels.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Reusing sixty percent means a lock necessarily withdraws sixty percent less water than any older lock."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b293-v15-35","title":"水位偏差與庫容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level bias and storage error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位偏差與庫容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level bias and storage error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。核對池位與外部流量表的完整循環差量，保留水面波動區間，不把平均後的小散布當成零偏差證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty. Reconcile full-cycle storage changes with external meters and retain surface-oscillation ranges rather than treating a small averaged scatter as evidence of no bias. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。核對池位與外部流量表的完整循環差量，保留水面波動區間，不把平均後的小散布當成零偏差證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty. Reconcile full-cycle storage changes with external meters and retain surface-oscillation ranges rather than treating a small averaged scatter as evidence of no bias.","failure":"注意干擾：兩支儀器接同一錯誤基準時讀值一致仍可能一起錯，重新校零前後的跳變也可能被誤認為節水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two sensors sharing an incorrect datum can agree while both are wrong, and a recalibration jump may resemble improved saving. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。核對池位與外部流量表的完整循環差量，保留水面波動區間，不把平均後的小散布當成零偏差證據。","textEn":"Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty. Reconcile full-cycle storage changes with external meters and retain surface-oscillation ranges rather than treating a small averaged scatter as evidence of no bias.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。核對池位與外部流量表的完整循環差量，保留水面波動區間，不把平均後的小散布當成零偏差證據。","textEn":"Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty. Reconcile full-cycle storage changes with external meters and retain surface-oscillation ranges rather than treating a small averaged scatter as evidence of no bias.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位偏差與庫容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level bias and storage error\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","每日蒸發方量應隨當天通航次數再乘一次作為總損失。","以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Daily evaporation volume must be multiplied again by the day's number of lockages.","Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以獨立穩定基準檢查水位零點，將兩儀器共用基準與獨立誤差分開。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check level zero against independent stable control, separating shared datum error from independent sensor uncertainty. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b293-v15-36","title":"水位偏差與庫容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level bias and storage error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位偏差與庫容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level bias and storage error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩支儀器接同一錯誤基準時讀值一致仍可能一起錯，重新校零前後的跳變也可能被誤認為節水。將誤差除以樣本數會虛構不合理的庫容精度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two sensors sharing an incorrect datum can agree while both are wrong, and a recalibration jump may resemble improved saving. Dividing systematic error by sample count invents unwarranted precision in the calculated storage volume. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固定水面6000m²、共同水位偏差0.010m，庫容偏差Aδz=60m³；此系統偏差不隨讀值數增加自動消失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Storage bias Aδz=60m³; additional readings do not automatically eliminate this systematic error.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩支水位儀讀值一致就能排除共同高程基準偏差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Agreement between two level sensors rules out any shared vertical-datum bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩支儀器接同一錯誤基準時讀值一致仍可能一起錯，重新校零前後的跳變也可能被誤認為節水。將誤差除以樣本數會虛構不合理的庫容精度。","textEn":"Two sensors sharing an incorrect datum can agree while both are wrong, and a recalibration jump may resemble improved saving. Dividing systematic error by sample count invents unwarranted precision in the calculated storage volume.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位偏差與庫容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level bias and storage error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩支儀器接同一錯誤基準時讀值一致仍可能一起錯，重新校零前後的跳變也可能被誤認為節水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["Two sensors sharing an incorrect datum can agree while both are wrong, and a recalibration jump may resemble improved saving.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩支儀器接同一錯誤基準時讀值一致仍可能一起錯，重新校零前後的跳變也可能被誤認為節水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two sensors sharing an incorrect datum can agree while both are wrong, and a recalibration jump may resemble improved saving. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b293-v15-37","title":"池體停用與供水韌性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Basin outage and supply resilience: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「池體停用與供水韌性」如何影響閘室節水池設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Basin outage and supply resilience” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-saving basins for lock chambers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"池體檢修或連通失效會改變可達回用率，外部補水增加幅度並不等於回用率減少的百分點。水源調度還受每日通航、庫存和其他用途限制，不能假設取水可無限補足；比較情境時應固定總交換需求，再清楚列出缺少哪些路徑。 假設每循環30000m³，回用率由0.60降0.40，外部補水由12000升18000m³，增加50%；非只增加20%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「池體停用與供水韌性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maintenance or a failed connection changes achievable reuse, and the percentage increase in makeup is not the percentage-point drop in reuse. Supply also depends on traffic, stored water and other demands, so unlimited replacement withdrawal cannot be assumed. Scenario comparison must hold gross exchange fixed while identifying missing pathways and any additional operational constraints. Assume gross exchange30000m³ per cycle. Reuse falls0.60to0.40; makeup rises12000to18000m³, a50% increase rather than20%. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Basin outage and supply resilience” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「池體停用與供水韌性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Basin outage and supply resilience”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-37-k1","title":"池體停用與供水韌性","titleEn":"Basin outage and supply resilience","text":"池體檢修或連通失效會改變可達回用率，外部補水增加幅度並不等於回用率減少的百分點。水源調度還受每日通航、庫存和其他用途限制，不能假設取水可無限補足；比較情境時應固定總交換需求，再清楚列出缺少哪些路徑。","textEn":"Maintenance or a failed connection changes achievable reuse, and the percentage increase in makeup is not the percentage-point drop in reuse. Supply also depends on traffic, stored water and other demands, so unlimited replacement withdrawal cannot be assumed.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「池體停用與供水韌性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Basin outage and supply resilience\" is correct?","options":["回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。","池體檢修或連通失效會改變可達回用率，外部補水增加幅度並不等於回用率減少的百分點。","浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。"],"optionsEn":["A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent.","Maintenance or a failed connection changes achievable reuse, and the percentage increase in makeup is not the percentage-point drop in reuse.","The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"池體檢修或連通失效會改變可達回用率，外部補水增加幅度並不等於回用率減少的百分點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maintenance or a failed connection changes achievable reuse, and the percentage increase in makeup is not the percentage-point drop in reuse. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b293-v15-38","title":"池體停用與供水韌性：定量估算","titleEn":"Basin outage and supply resilience: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「池體停用與供水韌性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Basin outage and supply resilience” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設每循環30000m³，回用率由0.60降0.40，外部補水由12000升18000m³，增加50%；非只增加20%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume gross exchange30000m³ per cycle. Reuse falls0.60to0.40; makeup rises12000to18000m³, a50% increase rather than20%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設每循環30000m³，回用率由0.60降0.40，外部補水由12000升18000m³，增加50%；非只增加20%。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume gross exchange30000m³ per cycle. Reuse falls0.60to0.40; makeup rises12000to18000m³, a50% increase rather than20%.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「池體停用與供水韌性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Basin outage and supply resilience\", which statement holds?","options":["節水池回收了多少比例的水就必然回收同樣比例的能量。","沒有船舶通過時節水池就不可能產生任何水量損失。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The fraction of water reused by a basin must equal the fraction of energy recovered.","A water-saving basin cannot lose water whenever no vessel is passing through the lock.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b293-v15-39","title":"池體停用與供水韌性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Basin outage and supply resilience: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「池體停用與供水韌性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Basin outage and supply resilience” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。核對水源、日庫存及額外漏損，不把模型餘額自動視為可供給量，並保存恢復連通前後的驗證證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand. Check source supply, daily storage and additional loss, without treating a calculated deficit as available water, and retain evidence before and after connection restoration. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。核對水源、日庫存及額外漏損，不把模型餘額自動視為可供給量，並保存恢復連通前後的驗證證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand. Check source supply, daily storage and additional loss, without treating a calculated deficit as available water, and retain evidence before and after connection restoration.","failure":"注意干擾：把回用率降低二十百分點誤當補水只增兩成，會低估檢修期水源需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking a twenty-point reuse reduction for twenty-percent more makeup understates maintenance demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。核對水源、日庫存及額外漏損，不把模型餘額自動視為可供給量，並保存恢復連通前後的驗證證據。","textEn":"Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand. Check source supply, daily storage and additional loss, without treating a calculated deficit as available water, and retain evidence before and after connection restoration.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。核對水源、日庫存及額外漏損，不把模型餘額自動視為可供給量，並保存恢復連通前後的驗證證據。","textEn":"Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand. Check source supply, daily storage and additional loss, without treating a calculated deficit as available water, and retain evidence before and after connection restoration.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「池體停用與供水韌性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Basin outage and supply resilience\"?","options":["列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","初始最大流量可以保持不變直到兩個池完全等水位。"],"optionsEn":["Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The initial maximum discharge remains unchanged until both basins have exactly equal levels."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列出停用池及仍可連通的路徑，用同一通航需求比較各狀態取水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map the unavailable basin and surviving connections, comparing withdrawals under identical traffic demand. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b293-v15-40","title":"池體停用與供水韌性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Basin outage and supply resilience: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"prerequisiteIds":["b293-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「池體停用與供水韌性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Basin outage and supply resilience” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把回用率降低二十百分點誤當補水只增兩成，會低估檢修期水源需求。若同時出現乾旱或鹽分沖洗需求，單一池停用可能放大整個通航系統的限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking a twenty-point reuse reduction for twenty-percent more makeup understates maintenance demand. Concurrent drought or salinity-flushing requirements can magnify the consequences of one unavailable basin for the wider navigation system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設每循環30000m³，回用率由0.60降0.40，外部補水由12000升18000m³，增加50%；非只增加20%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reuse falls0.60to0.40; makeup rises12000to18000m³, a50% increase rather than20%.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「回用率下降二十個百分點必然只讓外部補水增加百分之二十。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A twenty-percentage-point fall in reuse always increases external makeup by only twenty percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b293-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把回用率降低二十百分點誤當補水只增兩成，會低估檢修期水源需求。若同時出現乾旱或鹽分沖洗需求，單一池停用可能放大整個通航系統的限制。","textEn":"Mistaking a twenty-point reuse reduction for twenty-percent more makeup understates maintenance demand. Concurrent drought or salinity-flushing requirements can magnify the consequences of one unavailable basin for the wider navigation system.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]},{"id":"b293-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「池體停用與供水韌性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Basin outage and supply resilience\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把回用率降低二十百分點誤當補水只增兩成，會低估檢修期水源需求。","浮船排水量應在每次閘室升降方量中再完整扣除一次。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mistaking a twenty-point reuse reduction for twenty-percent more makeup understates maintenance demand.","The full floating-vessel displacement must be subtracted again from every chamber lift volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把回用率降低二十百分點誤當補水只增兩成，會低估檢修期水源需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking a twenty-point reuse reduction for twenty-percent more makeup understates maintenance demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v7-panama-basins","v15s-lock-hydraulics","v15s-lock-valves","v15s-acp-open"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
